              "text": "They all followed him into his dark hole, and they never came out again.",
              "audioStart": 121.763,
              "audioEnd": 125.188
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Long ago, the animals lived calm lives in the green land.",
              "audioStart": 126.05,
              "audioEnd": 129.262
            },
            {
              "text": "No one worried about the sky falling down.",
              "audioStart": 130.125,
              "audioEnd": 132.225
            },
            {
              "text": "Chicken Little was simply walking near the garden when the strange event occurred.",
              "audioStart": 133.088,
              "audioEnd": 136.625
            },
            {
              "text": "If she had not walked under that large tree, nothing would have happened to her soft head.",
              "audioStart": 137.488,
              "audioEnd": 141.787
            },
            {
              "text": "Many other birds joined the group as they ran along the road.",
              "audioStart": 142.65,
              "audioEnd": 145.5
            },
            {
              "text": "Each animal believed the frightening story without asking any questions.",
              "audioStart": 146.363,
              "audioEnd": 150.037
            },
            {
              "text": "They ran through the fields and past the forest because they wanted to stay alive.",
              "audioStart": 150.9,
              "audioEnd": 154.875
            },
            {
              "text": "If they had stayed at home, they would have been completely safe.",
              "audioStart": 155.738,
              "audioEnd": 158.787
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Foxy Loxy watched the large group of animals approach.",
              "audioStart": 159.65,
              "audioEnd": 162.65
            },
            {
              "text": "He knew that they were silly and easy to trick.",
              "audioStart": 163.512,
              "audioEnd": 165.825
            },
            {
              "text": "The brilliant leader smiled when he saw them running toward him.",
              "audioStart": 166.688,
              "audioEnd": 169.525
            },
            {
              "text": "He promised that his dark hole was a safe place.",
              "audioStart": 170.387,
              "audioEnd": 173.088
            },
            {
              "text": "If the animals had been smarter, they would have run away from him.",
              "audioStart": 173.95,
              "audioEnd": 177.012
            },
            {
              "text": "Instead, they walked right into his trap.",
              "audioStart": 177.875,
              "audioEnd": 180.175
            },
            {
              "text": "The door of the dark hole closed behind them, and they were never seen again.",
              "audioStart": 181.037,
              "audioEnd": 184.812
            },
            {
              "text": "That is why everyone should think carefully before believing strange stories.",
              "audioStart": 185.675,
              "audioEnd": 189.363
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Many days passed after the animals disappeared into the dark hole.",
              "audioStart": 190.225,
              "audioEnd": 193.65
            },
            {
              "text": "The green garden remained quiet and empty.",
              "audioStart": 194.512,
              "audioEnd": 196.662
            },
            {
              "text": "Other birds often talked about what had happened near the large tree.",
              "audioStart": 197.525,
              "audioEnd": 200.838
            },
            {
              "text": "If they had known the truth, they would have avoided the same mistake.",
              "audioStart": 201.7,
              "audioEnd": 204.925
            },
            {
              "text": "Life continued in the country, but the story was remembered by everyone.",
              "audioStart": 205.787,
              "audioEnd": 209.588
            },
            {
              "text": "Whenever the wind blew through the trees, people thought about Chicken Little.",
              "audioStart": 210.45,
              "audioEnd": 213.938
            },
            {
              "text": "They learned that listening to crazy reports without proof can lead to great danger.",
              "audioStart": 214.8,
              "audioEnd": 218.85
            },
            {
              "text": "That is why making careful choices is always important in life.",
              "audioStart": 219.713,
              "audioEnd": 223.125
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Sometimes people hear news that sounds very frightening.",
              "audioStart": 223.988,
              "audioEnd": 226.7
            },
            {
              "text": "If the news is not true, one should not panic or run away.",
              "audioStart": 227.562,
              "audioEnd": 230.85
            },
            {
              "text": "Instead, people must stop and think about the situation clearly.",
              "audioStart": 231.713,
              "audioEnd": 235.225
            },
            {
              "text": "Asking questions can help save a person from serious trouble.",
              "audioStart": 236.088,
              "audioEnd": 239.4
            },
            {
              "text": "If Chicken Little had asked more questions, she would not have scared all her friends.",
              "audioStart": 240.262,
              "audioEnd": 244.625
            },
            {
              "text": "Instead of running away, she should have looked up at the sky again.",
              "audioStart": 245.488,
              "audioEnd": 248.625
            },
            {
              "text": "Then she would have known that the sky was not falling down at all.",
              "audioStart": 249.488,
              "audioEnd": 252.438
            },
            {
              "text": "Every story needs careful attention before anyone believes it.",
              "audioStart": 253.3,
              "audioEnd": 256.575
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "The dark forest was a place where danger could hide easily.",
              "audioStart": 257.438,
              "audioEnd": 260.562
            },
            {
              "text": "Animals walked through the trees without knowing the risks.",
              "audioStart": 261.532,
              "audioEnd": 264.307
            },
            {
              "text": "If Foxy Loxy had not been waiting there, the group would have been fine.",
              "audioStart": 265.17,
              "audioEnd": 268.894
            },
            {
              "text": "Bad leaders often try to trick others into following them.",
              "audioStart": 269.757,
              "audioEnd": 272.732
            },
            {
              "text": "If someone offers you a quick way out of trouble, be very careful.",
              "audioStart": 273.594,
              "audioEnd": 277.07
            },
            {
              "text": "Smart people always check the facts before they make a decision.",
              "audioStart": 277.932,
              "audioEnd": 281.157
            },
            {
              "text": "That is the best lesson to learn from the tale of Chicken Little.",
              "audioStart": 282.019,
              "audioEnd": 284.995
            },
            {
              "text": "May everyone remember this story when they hear something strange.",
              "audioStart": 285.857,
              "audioEnd": 288.957
            }
          ]
        }
